COPY public.legal_guidance (crime_id, crime_type, applicable_laws, punishment, jurisdiction) FROM stdin;
1	Financial Fraud / UPI Scam	{"Section 66D, IT Act 2000 - Cheating by personation using computer resources","Section 420, IPC - Cheating and dishonestly inducing delivery of property","Section 43, IT Act - Unauthorized access and data theft"}	Imprisonment up to 3 years and/or fine up to â‚¹1 lakh	Local Cyber Crime Police Station or Judicial Magistrate Court
2	Social Media Harassment / Defamation	{"Section 67, IT Act 2000 - Publishing obscene material electronically","Section 499 & 500, IPC - Defamation","Section 507, IPC - Criminal intimidation by anonymous communication"}	Up to 3 years imprisonment and/or fine	Cyber Crime Police Station or Womenâ€™s Police Station
3	Identity Theft / Fake Profiles	{"Section 66C, IT Act 2000 - Identity theft","Section 468, IPC - Forgery for cheating","Section 471, IPC - Using forged document as genuine"}	Up to 3 years imprisonment and fine up to â‚¹1 lakh	\N
4	Online Extortion / Blackmail	{"Section 384, IPC - Extortion","Section 503, IPC - Criminal intimidation","Section 67A, IT Act - Publishing sexually explicit content"}	Imprisonment up to 7 years and fine	Local Cyber Police and Magistrate Court
5	Cyber Stalking	{"Section 354D, IPC - Stalking","Section 66E, IT Act - Violation of privacy"}	Imprisonment up to 3 years for first conviction	\N
6	Child Exploitation / CSAM	{"POCSO Act, 2012","Section 67B, IT Act - Child sexually explicit content","Section 292, IPC - Obscene publications"}	Up to 7 years imprisonment and fine	\N
7	Fake Loan / App Scams	{"Section 66D, IT Act - Cheating using communication devices","Section 420, IPC - Cheating","RBI Guidelines for Digital Lending, 2022"}	Up to 3 years imprisonment and fine	\N
\.
COPY public.reporting_procedures (report_id, crime_type, priority, procedure, contact_method, contact_detail, source) FROM stdin;
1	Financial Fraud / UPI Scam	URGENT (Call Immediately)	If you lose money through an online payment app, UPI transfer, or bank fraud, call 1930 immediately to request a transaction freeze before it is withdrawn.	Phone	1930	National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal (https://cybercrime.gov.in)
2	Social Media Harassment or Cyber Bullying	HIGH (Report Online)	If someone is threatening, blackmailing, or spreading false content through social media, take screenshots and URLs, and file a report on the National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal.	Website	https://cybercrime.gov.in	National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal
3	Online Sexual Exploitation or Child Abuse (CSAM)	URGENT (Report Immediately)	Report any explicit or abusive online content involving minors immediately through the 'Women/Child Related Crimes' section of the National Cyber Portal.	Website	https://cybercrime.gov.in	National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal
4	Identity Theft / Fake Social Media Profile	HIGH (Report Online)	If your photo, account, or identity is misused on any digital platform, report the account to the platform and then lodge a complaint on the Cyber Crime Portal.	Website	https://cybercrime.gov.in	National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal
5	Online Shopping / Delivery Fraud	MEDIUM (Report if Not Resolved)	If you paid online for goods or services and were cheated, contact the platformâ€™s support first. If unresolved, register a cyber fraud complaint online.	Website	https://cybercrime.gov.in	National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal
6	Hacking / Ransomware Attack	URGENT (Preserve Evidence & Report)	Disconnect your device from the internet immediately. Do not delete any files or messages. Report to your nearest Cyber Crime Police Station for assistance.	Local Police Station	See cybercells.json	Kerala Police Cyber Operations
7	Loan App / Data Misuse Complaint	HIGH (Report Online)	If you are being harassed or your data is misused by an unapproved loan app, report on the portal with screenshots and app details.	Website	https://cybercrime.gov.in	National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal
\.
COPY public.scam_advisories (scam_id, scam_name, keywords, modus_operandi, recent_intel, police_advice) FROM stdin;
1	Online Job Fraud / Money Mule Trap	job, work from home, telegram, mule, commission, trading	Fraudsters offer online jobs paying commissions. Later, they ask victims to use their bank accounts for fund transfers linked to cyber scams.	Kerala Police identified several Telegram job groups recruiting students for illegal fund transfers.	Do not share your bank details or act as a 'money mule'. Verify job offers on official company websites.
2	UPI / OTP Banking Fraud	OTP, bank, KYC, UPI, blocked, reward points	Scammers pose as bank staff, ask for OTP or UPI PIN, or send fake KYC links to steal money.	Cases reported in Ernakulam and Thiruvananthapuram where fraudsters cloned SIM cards using OTP.	Banks never ask for OTP or PIN. Do not share codes or click unknown links.
3	Fake Investment / Crypto Scam	crypto, trading, forex, bitcoin, profit, app	Fake trading apps and Telegram groups promise high returns. Victims are tricked into transferring funds to foreign wallets.	Kerala Cyber Cell warned against fake crypto investment apps circulating on social media.	Use only SEBI/RBI-registered platforms. Avoid investment offers through Telegram or Instagram.
4	E-commerce / Fake Website Fraud	shopping, delivery, fake, online store, payment, Amazon, Flipkart	Scammers create duplicate shopping sites. Payments are taken, but goods are never delivered or are fake.	Fake shopping domains reported in Kochi and Kozhikode linked to social media ads.	Shop only on verified websites with HTTPS and real customer reviews.
5	Instant Loan App Blackmail	loan, credit, app, personal data, harassment, gallery	Fake loan apps access contacts and photos, then blackmail victims to repay inflated amounts.	Thrissur and Palakkad victims faced threats from illegal Chinese-linked loan apps.	Install only RBI-approved apps. Revoke app permissions that access personal data.
6	Electricity Bill / Service SMS Scam	electricity, bill, payment, SMS, KSEB, disconnection	Fake messages claim your power will be disconnected and include malicious payment links.	Kerala Police warned users about fraudulent â€˜KSEB paymentâ€™ links stealing card details.	Ignore suspicious payment links. Use the official KSEB website for bill payments.
7	Online Romance / Dating Scam	dating, romance, relationship, gift, customs, money transfer	Scammers form online relationships, then claim emergencies or customs fees to extract money.	Cases in Kerala where victims lost large sums to romance scammers on dating apps.	Do not share personal photos or money with online acquaintances.
\.
